      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be pretty cool. Would save avatar makers and most players a ton of time by only having to make one prop rather than remaking it each time they want to include it on an avatar.\n\nI could see this also being useful with the new economy system where people could buy premade props to gain access to them in their inventory.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-12-27T23:35:36.212Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Items in VRChat are currently very limited! To use a simple prop like a lighter or a cellphone, one must add it to an avatar, add it to a world (and be in it), or find a world with that specific item.\n\nThis causes a lack of ′permanence′, which for example makes any games you complete feel more hollow! There is no permanent reward you can take and show. It also adds friction to self expression, something the platform aims to enable.\n\nI suggest an item inventory! Small, optimised props may be spawned by worlds or copied from others in exactly the same way as avatars are. They can then be stored/saved in the same way. The creator could also make them private or public so that prize props are kept ′special′. Ideally they′d be attachable to bones as they are already in some worlds!\n\nThese could be uploaded through the site and then referenced as part of worlds with a new ′prop′ object property. They′d be subject to limitations such as max saved props, max filesize, poly/shader count, etc. You could also limit a user to spawning a maximum amount, say 3, to keep things running smoothly. World creators could also prevent the spawning of personal items where it may not fit with their world!\n\nSeems like a logical next step in maturing the game, since one of the largest holes currently is lack of permanence outside instances :>",
